From ee21cb492b98eb2f2e8e4191314ada05487829b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:41:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add account deletion page for Play Console Data Safety
 requirement

Play Console's Data Safety form wants a reachable URL describing how
users can request account/data deletion, and EduQuinn didn't have one -
only a line in the privacy policy pointing at general Support contact.

- public/delete-account.html: explains how to request deletion (a
  pre-filled Support ticket), what gets removed, and what has to be kept
  (completed orders/payouts for tax records, security logs, other users'
  copies of messages/reviews, issued certificates) and why, plus notes
  for instructor accounts and parent/guardian requests.
- public/support.html: added an "Account deletion" topic option, and
  ?topic=&subject=&message= query-param pre-fill so the new page's link
  lands with the right ticket already drafted.
- Linked from the homepage footer and the privacy policy's "Your choices
  and rights" section.
- Updated PLAY-CONSOLE-CHECKLIST.md with the exact URL to paste into the
  Data Safety form, and noted this is a web page + support ticket, not an
  in-app self-service delete flow, in case review wants the stronger one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0117Yza2cLL621d3pHBjry2q
