+<!doctype html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="utf-8">
+  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
+  <title>Delete Your Account — EduQuinn</title>
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
+  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any"><link rel="icon" href="/app-icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png"><link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.webmanifest"><meta name="theme-color" content="#702632">
+</head>
+
+<body>
+
+<main class="policy-page">
+
+  <div class="policy-card">
+
+    <a href="/" class="policy-brand">
+      <span class="brand-mark">EQ</span>
+      <strong>EduQuinn</strong>
+    </a>
+
+    <h1>Delete Your Account</h1>
+
+    <p class="policy-updated">
+      Last updated: November 2026
+    </p>
+
+    <p>
+      This page explains how to request deletion of your EduQuinn account and
+      personal data, and what that does and doesn't remove. It applies
+      whether you use EduQuinn on the web at eduquinn.co.zw or through the
+      EduQuinn Android app.
+    </p>
+
+    <h2>1. How to request deletion</h2>
+    <p>
+      EduQuinn does not yet have a self-service "delete my account" button
+      inside the app, so a request currently goes through our support team:
+    </p>
+    <p>
+      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/support.html?topic=Account+deletion&amp;subject=Please+delete+my+EduQuinn+account&amp;message=Please+delete+my+EduQuinn+account+and+associated+personal+data.%0A%0AAccount+email%3A%0A">Request account deletion</a>
+    </p>
+    <p>
+      That opens our Support form with the topic and subject pre-filled —
+      just confirm the email address on your account and submit. You can
+      also email us directly; see the <a href="/support.html">Support</a>
+      page for the current address. Send the request from the email address
+      on your account where possible, so we can verify it's you.
+    </p>
+
+    <h2>2. What gets deleted</h2>
+    <ul>
+      <li>Your profile information: name, email address, password hash, and (for instructors) expertise/bio fields.</li>
+      <li>Your learning activity: course progress, quiz and assessment results, wishlist, and in-app messages you sent.</li>
+      <li>Any profile photo or coursework file you uploaded.</li>
+      <li>Your active login sessions, immediately.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p>We aim to complete deletion within 30 days of confirming your request.</p>
+
+    <h2>3. What we may have to keep</h2>
+    <p>
+      Some records can't be deleted immediately because we're required to
+      keep them for accounting, tax, or dispute-resolution purposes, or
+      because deleting them would affect other people's records:
+    </p>
+    <ul>
+      <li><strong>Completed order and payout records</strong> — kept for the period required by Zimbabwean tax and accounting law, with your name/email retained only as far as those records require.</li>
+      <li><strong>Security and audit logs</strong> of account activity — kept for a limited period for fraud and abuse prevention, then purged on the normal schedule.</li>
+      <li><strong>Messages you sent to another user, or a course review you left</strong> — the other party's copy of a conversation or an existing review is not deleted, but it will show as from a removed/deleted account rather than your name.</li>
+      <li><strong>Certificates already issued</strong> for completed courses remain independently verifiable (see <a href="/verify-certificate.html">Verify certificate</a>), since employers and institutions may rely on them — the certificate record is anonymised of everything except the credential itself unless you ask us to remove it entirely, which may affect your ability to prove you earned it.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>4. Instructor accounts</h2>
+    <p>
+      If you're an instructor with unresolved earnings or an open payout, we
+      will contact you to settle those first — deleting the account does not
+      cancel money already owed to or by you. Courses you published are
+      transferred to an "inactive instructor" state rather than deleted
+      outright, so enrolled students keep access to content they already
+      paid for; your personal profile information is still removed as
+      described above.
+    </p>
+
+    <h2>5. A parent or guardian requesting deletion for a minor</h2>
+    <p>
+      If you're a parent or guardian requesting deletion of a learner's
+      account on their behalf, use the same request form and note your
+      relationship to the learner in the message — we may ask for
+      reasonable verification before acting on the request.
+    </p>
+
+    <p class="policy-updated">
+      See our <a href="/privacy-policy.html">Privacy Policy</a> for the full
+      picture of what we collect and why. This page is a practical summary,
+      not a substitute for that policy.
+    </p>
+
+  </div>
+
+</main>
+
+</body>
+</html>
